From: Xinghe Defense Group <ops@xh-defense.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm439-xiaomi-pine: fix SD card detection

The microSD slot on Xiaomi Redmi 7A (pine) is not detected at all under
mainline: mmc@7864900 (SDC2) probes, but every attempt to talk to the card
times out (CMD8/CMD5 -> -110) and no mmcblk1 is created.

Root cause: the board drives the SD slot I/O at 3.3 V, but vqmmc-supply
points at pm8953_l12, which is limited to 1.8 V
(regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>). With the I/O rail at 1.8 V the card
never receives valid commands.

Fix: use the 3.3 V rail (pm8953_l11, already used for vmmc) for vqmmc as
well, forbid 1.8 V signalling with no-1-8-v, and rely on polling with
broken-cd since the card-detect IRQ never fires on this board.

Tested on Xiaomi Redmi 7A (pine), postmarketOS edge, kernel 7.1.3-msm89x7.
Without the patch there is no /dev/mmcblk1; with it:

  mmc1: new high speed SDHC card at address 0001
  mmcblk1: mmc1:0001 SD16G 29.8 GiB
   mmcblk1: p1

Signed-off-by: Xinghe Defense Group <ops@xh-defense.local>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm439-xiaomi-pine.dts | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm439-xiaomi-pine.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm439-xiaomi-pine.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm439-xiaomi-pine.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm439-xiaomi-pine.dts
@@ -293,7 +293,14 @@ &sdhc_2 {
 	cd-gpios = <&tlmm 67 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 	vmmc-supply = <&pm8953_l11>;
-	vqmmc-supply = <&pm8953_l12>;
+	/*
+	 * The SD slot I/O is 3.3 V on this board. pm8953_l12 is limited to
+	 * 1.8 V, so the card never answers CMD8/CMD5 and is not detected.
+	 * Use the 3.3 V rail and forbid 1.8 V signalling.
+	 */
+	vqmmc-supply = <&pm8953_l11>;
+	no-1-8-v;
+	broken-cd;
 	pinctrl-0 = <&sdc2_default &sdc2_cd_default>;
 	pinctrl-1 = <&sdc2_sleep &sdc2_cd_default>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
